{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CevgDBTzTDf3yWCZFBJCJn","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found excellent implementations. Here are the key patterns for line-by-line processing with bufio.Scanner/Reader:\n\n## Key Patterns for Line-by-Line Processing\n\n### 1. **Reading Lines with bufio.ReadBytes('\\n')** (head/main.go)\n```go\nbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\nfor range n {\n    line, err := br.ReadBytes('\\n')\n    if len(line) > 0 {\n        if _, werr := w.Write(line); werr != nil {\n            return werr\n        }\n    }\n    if err != nil {\n        return nil  // or handle io.EOF\n    }\n}\n```\n- Preserves the newline character in the line\n- Checks `len(line) > 0` to handle final lines without newlines\n- Returns `nil` on `io.EOF` (normal termination)\n\n### 2. **Stateful Line Processing with Buffered Writer** (cat/main.go)\n```go\nbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\nw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\nvar readErr error\nfor {\n    line, err := br.ReadBytes('\\n')\n    if len(line) > 0 {\n        lineNum, prevBlank = writeLine(w, line, lineNum, prevBlank)\n    }\n    if err != nil {\n        if err != io.EOF {\n            readErr = err\n        }\n        break\n    }\n}\nif ferr := w.Flush(); ferr != nil {\n    return lineNum, prevBlank, ferr\n}\nreturn lineNum, prevBlank, readErr\n```\n- Uses `bufio.NewWriter` for buffered output with eventual flush\n- Maintains state across lines (lineNum, prevBlank)\n- Always flushes before returning (catches write errors)\n- Separates read errors from EOF\n\n### 3. **Chunk Processing (when line-by-line isn't efficient)** (wc/main.go)\n```go\nbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\nbuf := make([]byte, 32*1024)\nfor {\n    n, err := br.Read(buf)\n    c.bytes += int64(n)\n    processChunk(buf[:n], &c, &inWord, &lineLen)\n    if err == io.EOF {\n        break\n    }\n    if err != nil {\n        return c, err\n    }\n}\n```\n- Reads chunks for stateful byte-level processing\n- Processes UTF-8 runes within chunks with `utf8.DecodeRune()`\n\n### 4. **Error Handling Pattern**\n- Distinguish between `io.EOF` (expected) and other errors\n- For stdout writes: return the error immediately (SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`)\n- For multiple files: accumulate errors, set exit code 1, but continue processing\n\n### 5. **File Handling Boilerplate**\n```go\nvar r io.Reader\nif name == \"-\" {\n    r = os.Stdin\n} else {\n    f, err := os.Open(name)\n    if err != nil {\n        return nil, nil, err\n    }\n    defer f.Close()\n    r = f\n}\n```\n\n**Summary**: Use `bufio.NewReader` + `ReadBytes('\\n')` for line-oriented processing, maintain state across iterations, buffer output with `bufio.NewWriter`, always flush before returning, and handle EOF separately from errors."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec5b32f0-bb5d-4262-aa9f-93da8741bdb1","uuid":"ef9deac8-41ea-4cf8-8894-3bad52e2d909","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:03:30.732Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5281, look at a few completed cmd/ implementations to see the typical pattern for line-by-line processing with bufio.Scanner. Check cmd/head/main.go, cmd/tail/main.go, or cmd/paste/main.go - whichever exists and has actual implementations (not just panic stubs). Show me the key patterns: how they read lines, write output, handle errors. Keep it brief - just the relevant code patterns.","agentId":"ab23bbd6645885dea","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found excellent implementations. Here are the key patterns for line-by-line processing with bufio.Scanner/Reader:\n\n## Key Patterns for Line-by-Line Processing\n\n### 1. **Reading Lines with bufio.ReadBytes('\\n')** (head/main.go)\n```go\nbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\nfor range n {\n    line, err := br.ReadBytes('\\n')\n    if len(line) > 0 {\n        if _, werr := w.Write(line); werr != nil {\n            return werr\n        }\n    }\n    if err != nil {\n        return nil  // or handle io.EOF\n    }\n}\n```\n- Preserves the newline character in the line\n- Checks `len(line) > 0` to handle final lines without newlines\n- Returns `nil` on `io.EOF` (normal termination)\n\n### 2. **Stateful Line Processing with Buffered Writer** (cat/main.go)\n```go\nbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\nw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\nvar readErr error\nfor {\n    line, err := br.ReadBytes('\\n')\n    if len(line) > 0 {\n        lineNum, prevBlank = writeLine(w, line, lineNum, prevBlank)\n    }\n    if err != nil {\n        if err != io.EOF {\n            readErr = err\n        }\n        break\n    }\n}\nif ferr := w.Flush(); ferr != nil {\n    return lineNum, prevBlank, ferr\n}\nreturn lineNum, prevBlank, readErr\n```\n- Uses `bufio.NewWriter` for buffered output with eventual flush\n- Maintains state across lines (lineNum, prevBlank)\n- Always flushes before returning (catches write errors)\n- Separates read errors from EOF\n\n### 3. **Chunk Processing (when line-by-line isn't efficient)** (wc/main.go)\n```go\nbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\nbuf := make([]byte, 32*1024)\nfor {\n    n, err := br.Read(buf)\n    c.bytes += int64(n)\n    processChunk(buf[:n], &c, &inWord, &lineLen)\n    if err == io.EOF {\n        break\n    }\n    if err != nil {\n        return c, err\n    }\n}\n```\n- Reads chunks for stateful byte-level processing\n- Processes UTF-8 runes within chunks with `utf8.DecodeRune()`\n\n### 4. **Error Handling Pattern**\n- Distinguish between `io.EOF` (expected) and other errors\n- For stdout writes: return the error immediately (SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`)\n- For multiple files: accumulate errors, set exit code 1, but continue processing\n\n### 5. **File Handling Boilerplate**\n```go\nvar r io.Reader\nif name == \"-\" {\n    r = os.Stdin\n} else {\n    f, err := os.Open(name)\n    if err != nil {\n        return nil, nil, err\n    }\n    defer f.Close()\n    r = f\n}\n```\n\n**Summary**: Use `bufio.NewReader` + `ReadBytes('\\n')` for line-oriented processing, maintain state across iterations, buffer output with `bufio.NewWriter`, always flush before returning, and handle EOF separately from errors."}],"totalDurationMs":13306,"totalTokens":29455,"totalToolUseCount":4,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10133,"cache_read_input_tokens":18470,"output_tokens":846,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10133},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":18470,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10133,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10133,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":3,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
